        "id": "baby-diaper-conversation",
        "kind": "everyday-situation",
        "title": "A conversation during a diaper change",
        "summary": "Tell your baby what is happening during a needed change, using gentle touch and ordinary words for their body. Their response can be part of the exchange.",
        "cue": "A diaper needs changing.",
        "detail": [
          "The authors describe diapering as private, respectful care. They name what has happened without calling the baby dirty or making a disgusted face.",
          "They explain the next action and leave room for a response or a small movement. The adult still provides the care the baby needs.",
          "In the home-setup passage, they keep supplies ready and always keep a hand on the baby at a raised changing surface."
        ],
